  "answer": "The implementation is complete. Let me summarize what was done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `mergeRanges(ranges)` in `ranges.mjs`, keeping the named export.\n\n### Behavior implemented\n\n**Validation (throws `TypeError`):**\n- Input must be an array.\n- Each element must be a pair array of length exactly 2.\n- Both bounds must be safe integers (`Number.isSafeInteger`).\n- `start <= end` must hold.\n\n**Merging logic:**\n- Empty input returns `[]`.\n- Input is copied via `.map(([start, end]) => [start, end])` before sorting, so the original array and its pairs are never mutated.\n- Sorted by start, then end (`a[0] - b[0] || a[1] - b[1]`).\n- Intervals merge when they overlap **or touch as adjacent integers** (`range[0] <= last[1] + 1`), e.g. `[2,4]` + `[5,7]` → `[2,7]`.\n- Contained intervals don't shorten the current interval — the end is only extended when `range[1] > last[1]`.\n- Returns fresh pair arrays inside a fresh result array, sorted by start.\n\n### Key fixes over the original\nThe original code mutated the input (`ranges.sort(...)`, `last[1] = ...`), had no validation, and didn't handle adjacency (`[2,4]`/`[5,7]` would not merge). All of these are now addressed.\n\nThe two provided tests (`unsorted overlaps merge in order` and `adjacent integer intervals touch`) are satisfied by this implementation.",
